  "description": "GC regression pin for content-merge ownership during parse(): list_push's S2.6.4 merge of adjacent strings took the script's eval context (input_context) for the owner, so the Markdown parser's merged text runs were heap strings inside an arena-owned element nothing traces, swept at the next collection. The value of this fixture is the forced-collection stress sweep (test_mir_gc_stress_gtest: LAMBDA_GC_FORCE_EVERY=1 + LAMBDA_GC_POISON_FREED=1 on every tier), where the runs read back poisoned, or as a neighbouring string, before an active input parse owned its merged text. The emission check only pins that the churn helper's record literal is lowered as a typed map literal rather than a generic map_put chain, so the allocation pressure it supplies stays what the stress sweep was tuned with.",
